    "media:imagetext": "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nIn the mountains north of Peking (Beijing), looking toward Inner Mongolia, is the Great Wall. The largest\nman-made structure on earth, the 3,000 mile wall was begun in the third century B.C. It took over\n200 years to complete. The Peking area also offers such wondrous sights as the Ming Tombs, the\nForbidden City, the Great Hall, Chairman Mao's Memorial and the Temple of Heaven. Shanghai,\nSoochow (Suzhou), Hangchow (Hangzhou), and Canton (Guangzhou), among many other cities,\noffer equally breathtaking vistas.\nA visit to the People's Republic of China is a unique and totally remarkable experience; now, only\n14 hours away on Pan Am's 747SP Clippers.\nOPAN AM\n2007.054.006",
