    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktails\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nStenus\nApéritif\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\n#:****\nRoast au Vol\nA selected cut of aged beef\nroasted on board and cared to order.\nSeafood Platter\nCold Lush Seafood with a Tangy Japanese Sauce\nBreast of Chicken Oriental\nTrout Grenobloise\nTrout Sauteed with Capers, Lemon, Butter and Fresh Parsley\nPlat du Jour\nSteamed Rice\nButtered Veaetable Bouauet",
      "Breast of Chicken Oriental\nTrout Grenobloise\nTrout Sauteed with Capers, Lemon, Butter and Fresh Parsley\n4: 2002\n**I.**\nPlat du Jour\nSteamed Rice\n1 z\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nCoffee\n]-E-\nPotatoes Maison\n*\nTossed Garden Salad\n$*»#\nSelection of Cheeses and Fruits\n******+\nDessert\nTV-A\nTea\nGreen Tea\n*\n• * *\nDecaffeinated Coffee\n3-E-\n**\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nContreau\n236.KJC001",
      "THE GREAT WALL OF CHINA\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nIn the mountains north of Peking (Beijing), looking toward Inner Mongolia, is the Great Wall. The largest\nman-made structure on earth, the 3,000 mile wall was begun in the third century B.C. It took over\n200 years to complete. The Peking area also offers such wondrous sights as the Ming Tombs, the\nForbidden City, the Great Hall, Chairman Mao's Memorial and the Temple of Heaven. Shanghai,\nSoochow (Suzhou), Hangchow (Hangzhou), and Canton (Guangzhou), among many other cities,\noffer equally breathtaking vistas.\nA visit to the People's Republic of China is a unique and totally remarkable experience; now, only\n14 hours away on Pan Am's 747SP Clippers.\nOPAN AM\n2007.054.006"
    ],
